---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PipelineFlow from '../components/PipelineFlow.astro';
import AnalysisFramework from '../components/AnalysisFramework.astro';
import ChannelCoverageMaps from '../components/ChannelCoverageMaps.astro';
import ChannelPatchAnalysis from '../components/ChannelPatchAnalysis.astro';
import ExposureFindings from '../components/ExposureFindings.astro';
import SpatialRobustness from '../components/SpatialRobustness.astro';

const facts = [
	{ value: '43k', label: 'LSOAs / Data Zones' },
	{ value: '16.5m', label: 'postcode–restaurant links' },
	{ value: '100k', label: 'restaurant profiles' },
	{ value: '1', label: 'major delivery platform' },
	{ value: '6', label: 'major grocery services' },
];
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Britain's Digital Food Environment"
	description="A spatial data project mapping restaurant and grocery delivery across Britain, from data engineering to demographic and statistical analysis."
	socialImage="og.png"
>
	<header class="site-header site-shell">
		<a class="wordmark" href="#overview">DFRE / Spatial data project</a>
		<nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
			<a href="#overview">Overview</a>
			<a href="#pipeline">Pipeline</a>
			<a href="#findings">Findings</a>
			<a href={`${base}explore/`}>Explore</a>
		</nav>
	</header>

	<main id="main-content">
		<section class="hero site-shell" id="overview">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Digital food retail environment · Great Britain</p>
				<h1>Mapping Britain's digital food environment</h1>
				<p class="hero-deck">
					An end-to-end spatial data project tracing how restaurant and grocery delivery vary across place. The analysis examines how these spatial patterns relate to deprivation, rurality and population.
				</p>
				<div class="hero-tags" aria-label="Project disciplines">
					<span>Data engineering</span>
					<span>Spatial analysis</span>
					<span>Spatial modelling</span>
					<span>Data visualisation</span>
				</div>
				<div class="hero-actions">
					<a class="primary-action" href={`${base}explore/`}>Explore the interactive map <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
					<a class="secondary-action" href="#findings">Read the findings</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<aside class="scale-note" aria-label="Dataset scale">
				<p>A national evidence base built from representative postcodes and area-level indicators.</p>
				{facts.map((fact) => (
					<div class="fact">
						<span class="fact-value">{fact.value}</span>
						<span class="fact-label">{fact.label}</span>
					</div>
				))}
			</aside>
		</section>

		<section class="pipeline-section site-shell" id="pipeline">
			<PipelineFlow />
		</section>

		<section class="analysis-framework-section site-shell" aria-label="Analysis overview">
			<AnalysisFramework />
		</section>

		<section class="finding-section channel-section" id="findings">
			<div class="site-shell">
				<div class="editorial-intro">
					<p class="section-kicker">Finding 01 · Retail network extension</p>
					<h2>Digital delivery platforms form an additional layer of local food retail reach.</h2>
					<p>Using Just Eat as the observed platform, the analysis compares retailer listings with matched retailer-owned services on a common small-area geography. It identifies where the two networks overlap and where the platform provides additional observed reach.</p>
				</div>
				<ChannelCoverageMaps />
				<ChannelPatchAnalysis />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="finding-section exposure-section">
			<div class="site-shell">
				<div class="editorial-intro">
					<p class="section-kicker">Finding 02 · Inequality in available food choice</p>
					<h2>Fast-food exposure varies with deprivation and rurality, but the estimated deprivation gradient is spatially sensitive.</h2>
					<p>Count, population-standardised density and fast-food share capture different dimensions of exposure. Adjusted non-spatial models retain a positive deprivation gradient, while the rural–urban contrast is strongest for the breadth of available restaurants. Spatial error sensitivities substantially weaken the IMD gradient, so it is treated as model-dependent rather than a definitive independent effect.</p>
				</div>
				<ExposureFindings />
				<SpatialRobustness />
			</div>
		</section>

	</main>

	<footer class="site-footer site-shell" id="contact">
		<div class="contact-identity">
			<p>Contact</p>
			<strong>Chenrui Xiao</strong>
		</div>
		<nav class="contact-links" aria-label="Contact links">
			<a href="mailto:chenruix.job@gmail.com">chenruix.job@gmail.com</a>
			<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/chenrui-xiao-940378205/" target="_blank" rel="me noreferrer">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/sipothemaster" target="_blank" rel="me noreferrer">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
		</nav>
	</footer>
</BaseLayout>
